# EtPopover Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtPopover` is a compound component for displaying contextual overlays attached to target elements. It provides:

- **Directional positioning**: Appears above, below, left, or right of the target
- **Arrow shown by default**: Arrow is automatically rendered unless `hideArrow` is set
- **Arrow alignment**: Arrow can be positioned at start, center, or end
- **Theme-aware colors**: Automatically inverts colors based on light/dark theme
- **Timing control**: Show delay and auto-hide functionality
- **Modal-based rendering**: Renders outside normal layout flow for proper positioning
- **RTL support**: Full right-to-left language support

**Does NOT handle:**

- Tooltip functionality (use this for richer content popovers)
- Complex forms or interactive content beyond simple buttons
- Nested popovers

## Entry Points & Contracts

### Compound Component Structure

```tsx
<EtPopover.Root>
  // Main wrapper - provides context
  <EtPopover.Target>
    // Wraps the element the popover points to
    {/* Target element */}
  </EtPopover.Target>
  <EtPopover.Content>
    // Contains popover content
    <EtPopover.Title /> // Optional title with icon
    <EtPopover.Text /> // Optional description text with icon
    <EtPopover.Button /> // Optional action button
    <EtPopover.CloseButton /> // Optional close button
    {/* Arrow is shown by default - no need to add <EtPopover.Arrow /> */}
  </EtPopover.Content>
</EtPopover.Root>
```

### `EtPopover.Root` (main wrapper)

```tsx
<EtPopover.Root
  visible?: boolean             // default: true - controls popover visibility
  popoverDirection?: PopoverDirection  // default: 'above'
  arrowAlignment?: PopoverArrowAlignment  // default: 'center'
  showDelay?: number            // default: 500 (milliseconds)
  autoHideDelay?: number        // default: 3000 (ms, 0 = no auto-hide)
  onClose?: () => void          // called on close/auto-hide
  closeOnOutsidePress?: boolean // default: true
  hideArrow?: boolean           // default: false - arrow is shown by default
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
/>
```

**Important defaults:**

- `visible={true}` - Popover is visible by default
- `showDelay={500}` - 500ms delay before showing
- `autoHideDelay={3000}` - Auto-hides after 3 seconds (set to `0` to disable)
- `hideArrow={false}` - Arrow is shown by default (set to `true` to hide it)

### `EtPopover.Target` (target wrapper)

```tsx
<EtPopover.Target
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
>
  {/* Your target element goes here */}
</EtPopover.Target>
```

### `EtPopover.Content` (content container)

Supports two APIs: **compound children** (traditional) and **props-based** (simpler).

#### Compound Children API (traditional)

```tsx
<EtPopover.Content
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
>
  {/* Title, Text, Button, CloseButton, Arrow */}
</EtPopover.Content>
```

#### Props-Based API (simpler)

```tsx
<EtPopover.Content
  title?: string | { text: string; iconName?: string; style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle> }
  text?: string | { text: string; iconName?: string; style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle> }
  button?: string | { label: string; onPress: () => void; style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle> }
  onButtonPress?: () => void      // Used when button is a string
  closeButton?: boolean | PopoverCloseButtonProps
  arrow?: boolean | PopoverArrowProps
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
/>
```

#### String Shorthand

```tsx
<EtPopover.Content>Simple text content as a string</EtPopover.Content>
```

### `EtPopover.Title` (title with optional icon)

```tsx
<EtPopover.Title
  iconName?: string  // optional icon before title
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
>
  {/* Title text (string) */}
</EtPopover.Title>
```

### `EtPopover.Text` (description text with optional icon)

```tsx
<EtPopover.Text
  iconName?: string  // optional icon before text
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
>
  {/* Description text (string) */}
</EtPopover.Text>
```

### `EtPopover.Button` (action button)

```tsx
<EtPopover.Button
  onPress: () => void  // required - press handler
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
>
  {/* Button label (string) */}
</EtPopover.Button>
```

### `EtPopover.CloseButton` (close button)

```tsx
<EtPopover.CloseButton
  onPress?: () => void  // optional - overrides context onClose
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
/>
```

### `EtPopover.Arrow` (arrow pointer - shown by default)

Arrow is **automatically rendered** by default. You only need to explicitly add `<EtPopover.Arrow />` if you want to customize its style. Use `hideArrow` prop on `EtPopover.Root` to hide it.

```tsx
// Arrow is shown automatically - no need to add this unless customizing
<EtPopover.Arrow
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
/>
```

### Types

| Type                    | Values                                                                             |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `PopoverDirection`      | `'above'` \| `'below'` \| `'left'` \| `'right'`                                    |
| `PopoverArrowAlignment` | `'start'` \| `'center'` \| `'end'`                                                 |
| `PopoverTitleConfig`    | `string` \| `{ text: string; iconName?: string; style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle> }`    |
| `PopoverTextConfig`     | `string` \| `{ text: string; iconName?: string; style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle> }`    |
| `PopoverButtonConfig`   | `string` \| `{ label: string; onPress: () => void; style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle> }` |

**Direction behavior:**

- `above`: Popover appears above target, arrow at bottom pointing down
- `below`: Popover appears below target, arrow at top pointing up
- `left`: Popover appears to left of target, arrow on right pointing right
- `right`: Popover appears to right of target, arrow on left pointing left

**Arrow alignment:**

- `start`: Arrow at the start edge (left in LTR, right in RTL)
- `center`: Arrow centered on the edge
- `end`: Arrow at the end edge (right in LTR, left in RTL)

