## Usage Patterns

### Basic popover with default behavior

By default, popover appears after 500ms delay, auto-hides after 3 seconds, and shows the arrow:

```tsx
<EtPopover.Root popoverDirection="above" onClose={() => console.log('Popover closed')}>
  <EtPopover.Target>
    <View style={styles.target} />
  </EtPopover.Target>
  <EtPopover.Content>
    <EtPopover.Title>Welcome!</EtPopover.Title>
    <EtPopover.Text>This tip will auto-hide in 3 seconds.</EtPopover.Text>
    <EtPopover.CloseButton />
    {/* Arrow is shown by default - no need to add <EtPopover.Arrow /> */}
  </EtPopover.Content>
</EtPopover.Root>
```

### Interactive popover with state control

For user-controlled visibility, disable auto-hide and manage state:

```tsx
const [visible, setVisible] = useState(false);

<EtPopover.Root
  visible={visible}
  popoverDirection="above"
  showDelay={0} // Show immediately
  autoHideDelay={0} // Don't auto-hide
  onClose={() => setVisible(false)}
>
  <EtPopover.Target>
    <Pressable onPress={() => setVisible(true)}>
      <EtText>Show Info</EtText>
    </Pressable>
  </EtPopover.Target>
  <EtPopover.Content>
    <EtPopover.Title>Welcome!</EtPopover.Title>
    <EtPopover.Text>This is a helpful tip for you.</EtPopover.Text>
    <EtPopover.CloseButton />
  </EtPopover.Content>
</EtPopover.Root>;
```

### Popover with action button

```tsx
<EtPopover.Root
  popoverDirection="below"
  autoHideDelay={0} // Disable auto-hide for action popovers
  onClose={() => setVisible(false)}
>
  <EtPopover.Target>
    <Button onPress={() => setVisible(true)}>Open Popover</Button>
  </EtPopover.Target>
  <EtPopover.Content>
    <EtPopover.Title>Confirm Action</EtPopover.Title>
    <EtPopover.Text>Are you sure you want to proceed?</EtPopover.Text>
    <EtPopover.Button onPress={handleConfirm}>Confirm</EtPopover.Button>
    <EtPopover.CloseButton />
  </EtPopover.Content>
</EtPopover.Root>
```

