### Props-based API (simpler alternative)

Instead of compound children, use props for a more concise syntax:

```tsx
// Simple text-only popover
<EtPopover.Content text="This is a helpful tip" arrow />

// With title and close button
<EtPopover.Content
  title="Welcome!"
  text="This is a helpful tip for you."
  closeButton
  arrow
/>

// With icons
<EtPopover.Content
  title={{ text: "Important Notice", iconName: "info" }}
  text={{ text: "Please read this carefully.", iconName: "warning" }}
  arrow
/>

// With action button (string shorthand)
<EtPopover.Content
  title="Confirm Action"
  text="Are you sure you want to proceed?"
  button="Confirm"
  onButtonPress={handleConfirm}
  closeButton
  arrow
/>

// With action button (config object)
<EtPopover.Content
  title="Confirm Action"
  text="Are you sure you want to proceed?"
  button={{ label: "Confirm", onPress: handleConfirm }}
  closeButton
  arrow
/>
```

### String shorthand for simple text

For text-only popovers, pass a string directly as children:

```tsx
<EtPopover.Content>Pro tip: Use keyboard shortcuts for faster navigation!</EtPopover.Content>
```

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Missing Target or Content

```tsx
// BAD - Target and Content are required
<EtPopover.Root visible={visible}>
  <EtPopover.Title>Hello</EtPopover.Title>
</EtPopover.Root>
```

**Fix:** Always wrap target element in `EtPopover.Target` and content in `EtPopover.Content`:

```tsx
<EtPopover.Root visible={visible}>
  <EtPopover.Target>
    <Button>Show</Button>
  </EtPopover.Target>
  <EtPopover.Content>
    <EtPopover.Title>Hello</EtPopover.Title>
    {/* Arrow is shown by default */}
  </EtPopover.Content>
</EtPopover.Root>
```

### ❌ Forgetting to disable auto-hide for interactive popovers

```tsx
// BAD - popover will auto-hide in 3 seconds while user is reading/interacting
<EtPopover.Root onClose={() => setVisible(false)}>
  <EtPopover.Content>
    <EtPopover.Title>Important Action</EtPopover.Title>
    <EtPopover.Text>Long text that needs time to read...</EtPopover.Text>
    <EtPopover.Button onPress={handleAction}>Take Action</EtPopover.Button>
  </EtPopover.Content>
</EtPopover.Root>
```

**Fix:** Disable auto-hide for popovers that require user interaction:

```tsx
<EtPopover.Root
  autoHideDelay={0} // Disable auto-hide
  onClose={() => setVisible(false)}
>
  ...
</EtPopover.Root>
```

### ❌ Using state when not needed

```tsx
// UNNECESSARY - for simple auto-hide popovers, state management is optional
const [visible, setVisible] = useState(true);
<EtPopover.Root visible={visible} onClose={() => setVisible(false)}>
  ...
</EtPopover.Root>;
```

**Simpler:** For auto-hide popovers that appear once, just use defaults:

```tsx
// visible defaults to true, auto-hides after 3 seconds
<EtPopover.Root onClose={() => console.log('closed')}>...</EtPopover.Root>
```

### ❌ Placing custom Arrow outside Content

Note: Arrow is now shown by default, so you don't need to add it. But if you want to customize it:

```tsx
// BAD - Custom Arrow must be inside Content
<EtPopover.Root visible={visible}>
  <EtPopover.Target>...</EtPopover.Target>
  <EtPopover.Content>
    <EtPopover.Title>Hello</EtPopover.Title>
  </EtPopover.Content>
  <EtPopover.Arrow style={{ ... }} />  {/* Wrong! */}
</EtPopover.Root>
```

**Fix:** Custom Arrow must be a child of Content (or use `hideArrow` prop to hide default arrow):

```tsx
// Option 1: Arrow is automatic - no need to add it
<EtPopover.Content>
  <EtPopover.Title>Hello</EtPopover.Title>
</EtPopover.Content>

// Option 2: Customize the arrow
<EtPopover.Content>
  <EtPopover.Title>Hello</EtPopover.Title>
  <EtPopover.Arrow style={{ marginTop: 4 }} />
</EtPopover.Content>

// Option 3: Hide the arrow
<EtPopover.Root hideArrow>
  <EtPopover.Content>
    <EtPopover.Title>Hello</EtPopover.Title>
  </EtPopover.Content>
</EtPopover.Root>
```

### ❌ Manually styling text/icon colors

```tsx
// BAD - colors are automatically managed by theme
<EtPopover.Title style={{ color: 'white' }}>Hello</EtPopover.Title>
```

**Fix:** Let the component manage colors automatically based on theme. Use `style` only for layout (margins, padding, etc.).

### ❌ Forgetting onClose handler

```tsx
// BAD - no way to close the popover
<EtPopover.Root visible={visible}>
  ...
  <EtPopover.CloseButton /> {/* Won't work without onClose */}
  ...
</EtPopover.Root>
```

**Fix:** Always provide `onClose` when using close functionality:

```tsx
<EtPopover.Root visible={visible} onClose={() => setVisible(false)}>
  ...
</EtPopover.Root>
```

### ❌ Using for complex forms

```tsx
// BAD - popovers are for simple content only
<EtPopover.Content>
  <TextInput />
  <CheckBox />
  <Button>Submit</Button>
</EtPopover.Content>
```

**Fix:** Use a bottom sheet or modal for complex interactive content.

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - provides theme colors for automatic dark/light mode handling
- `useTheme` from `@react-navigation/native` - provides `dark` flag for theme detection
- `EtText` - text rendering for title, text, and button labels
- `EtoroIcon` - icons for title, text, and close button (uses `iconColor` from context)
- Spacing constants from `core/styles/spacing` (X1, X3, X4, X5)

### External Dependencies

- `react-native` - `View`, `Pressable`, `Modal`, `StyleSheet`, `Dimensions`, `I18nManager`

### Design System Integration

- **Colors** (theme-aware, inverted from app theme):
  - Light mode app → Dark popover background with light text/icons
  - Dark mode app → Light popover background with dark text/icons
  - Uses semantic tokens `textPrimaryNeutral` (background) and `textInvertedPrimaryNeutral` (text/icons) which naturally invert
- **Typography**:
  - Title: `body-base-semibold`
  - Text: `body-base-regular`
  - Button: `label-tertiary-semibold`
- **Arrow**: 14x7px triangle with explicit container dimensions for flex layout
- **Layout**:
  - Min width: 250px
  - Max width: 350px
  - Padding: 20px (X5)
  - Border radius: 8px
  - Gap between elements: 4px (X1)

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Compound Component Pattern

`EtPopover` uses the compound component pattern:

- `Root` provides context to all children
- Subcomponents read from context for colors and state
- Content is restructured internally so it renders inside Target for proper positioning
- **Important**: Subcomponents are detected by `displayName`. When using `React.memo()`, the `displayName` must be set on BOTH the inner component AND the memo wrapper:

```tsx
function MySubcomponent() { ... }
MySubcomponent.displayName = 'EtPopover.MySubcomponent';

export const MySubcomponent = React.memo(MySubcomponentComponent);
MySubcomponent.displayName = 'EtPopover.MySubcomponent'; // Required!
```

### Positioning System

The popover uses Modal for rendering outside normal layout flow:

1. Target element is measured using `measureInWindow`
2. Popover position is calculated based on direction and alignment
3. Screen bounds are respected with automatic clamping

### Theme Inversion

Colors are automatically inverted based on theme:

- In light mode: popover has dark background with light text
- In dark mode: popover has light background with dark text

This ensures popovers always have good contrast against their content.

### Timing Control

The `usePopoverTiming` hook manages:

- **showDelay** (default: 500ms): Delays showing the popover after `visible` becomes true
- **autoHideDelay** (default: 3000ms): Automatically hides the popover after the specified duration

**Disabling timing:**

- Set `showDelay={0}` for instant display
- Set `autoHideDelay={0}` to disable auto-hide (popover stays until manually closed)

### RTL Support

Full RTL support is built-in:

- Arrow alignment respects logical directions (start/end)
- Horizontal positioning is RTL-aware
- Horizontal popovers use LTR direction to prevent layout flip issues

### Accessibility

Built-in accessibility features:

- Content container has `accessibilityRole="alert"` and `accessibilityViewIsModal`
- Close button and action button have proper accessibility roles
- Modal supports hardware back button for closing

## Troubleshooting

**Q: Popover not appearing**
A: Ensure both `Target` and `Content` are provided. Note: there's a 500ms default show delay

**Q: Popover disappears too quickly**
A: Default auto-hide is 3 seconds. Set `autoHideDelay={0}` to disable, or increase the value

**Q: Popover positioned incorrectly**
A: Check that target element has proper dimensions; ensure parent doesn't have overflow hidden

**Q: Arrow not showing**
A: Arrow is now shown by default. Check that `hideArrow` is not set to `true` on `EtPopover.Root`. If you need to customize the arrow, place `<EtPopover.Arrow style={...} />` inside `<EtPopover.Content>`

**Q: Close button not working**
A: Ensure `onClose` prop is provided to `Root`

**Q: Colors look wrong**
A: Don't override text/icon colors; let theme handle them automatically

**Q: Popover not closing on outside press**
A: Check `closeOnOutsidePress` prop (defaults to `true`)

